## Pairing discipline

Per `DEC-2026-05-17-003` Clause 1: every anti-pattern MUST be paired with a canonical pattern. The framework's value depends on showing the user *both* what to reject and what to do instead. Standalone anti-patterns without paired canonical patterns are incomplete and should not ship.

When a new anti-pattern is observed but no clear canonical pattern is obvious, log to `WAIVER-LOG.md` for revisit rather than shipping a one-sided entry.
